# A joined group whose stream arrives, stops and comes back. The counter of
# its MAC grows from second 4 to 9 (1000 bytes a second), then stands still:
# ten seconds after it last grew, at 19, the group is lost (the meter file
# says flow=lost and lost=1, the omcid alarm follows). It grows again at 25
# and the group flows again at once. The client and the time of the last
# join come from the reports: the second report, from another host, moves
# both.
0 policy
snooping=1
igmp_function=0
immediate_leave=1
end
0 tick
1 v2join 1 0 192.168.1.10 239.1.1.1
2 meter
3 ctr 239.1.1.1 1000
4 tick
4 ctr 239.1.1.1 2000
5 tick
5 ctr 239.1.1.1 3000
6 tick
6 ctr 239.1.1.1 4000
7 tick
7 ctr 239.1.1.1 5000
8 tick
8 ctr 239.1.1.1 6000
9 tick
10 meter
18 tick
18 meter
19 tick
19 meter
20 v2join 1 0 192.168.1.20 239.1.1.1
21 meter
24 ctr 239.1.1.1 6500
25 tick
